  {"kind": "narration", "speaker_id": null, "text": "In the Hearth, the evening light slants through the smoke-hazed windows as Wren leans in across the table, gesturing with one hand toward the door as if the rocky islets south of Corvane were just outside. Ash sets down a cup and watches, intent, the words hanging unfinished between them.", "cited_fact_keys": ["spots", "attempt:communicate", "previously"]},
  {"kind": "narration", "speaker_id": null, "text": "Wren tries again, tracing a rough line in the spilled ale on the wood — south, past the harbor — as they speak about what waits among those islets, the name Corvane falling like a stone into the quiet.", "cited_fact_keys": ["attempt:communicate", "reaction:1"]},
