  {"kind": "narration", "speaker_id": null, "text": "Evening gathers over the village, and the market square lies nearly empty, straw and dust drifting from the day's bustle. At the stone bridge, Ash waits, watching the dark water slide past, listening for Wren's footsteps.", "cited_fact_keys": ["place", "spots", "previously", "attempt:wait"]},
  {"kind": "dialogue", "speaker_id": "f01c6baf-0996-42fd-a9b9-4a97cb6a7af3", "text": "Wren joins Ash at the bridge. \"We spoke of the Fisher's Lost Catch before — let's look further now, to the rocky islets south of Corvane.\"", "cited_fact_keys": ["reaction:2", "attempt:communicate"]},
  {"kind": "narration", "speaker_id": null, "text": "Ash turns, their gaze sharpening, and replies about those islets — low, stone-ribbed lumps beyond the harbor, where the sea stacks hide narrow channels.", "cited_fact_keys": ["reaction:1"]},
  {"kind": "narration", "speaker_id": null, "text": "Wren leans on the worn rail, voice thoughtful, telling Ash again the old tale's turn, how the catch slips from any net near those rocks.", "cited_fact_keys": ["previously", "reaction:2"]}
]

